#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:826
#~ msgid ""
#~ "JP-style open play is the avoid-repeats baseline plus one intervention: a "
#~ "foursome is split when it is obviously lopsided — the pairs half a DUPR "
#~ "apart, the bar real organisers actually use. The surprise is that the "
#~ "intervention buys nothing measurable: JP lands within the error bars of "
#~ "its own baseline everywhere, a point or two of quality in this club at "
#~ "best. Splits that rare cannot move a session. Politeness that fixes only "
#~ "the egregious matches is worth almost nothing; the gains begin when every "
#~ "match is deliberately balanced, which is exactly what nobody does "
#~ "socially."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "日式开放打法是“避免重复”基线加上一项干预：当一组四人明显失衡时将其拆开——两"
#~ "对相差半个 DUPR，这正是真实组织者使用的标准。令人意外的是，这项干预没带来"
#~ "任何可测量的收益：日式打法在各处都落在其自身基线的误差范围内，在这个俱乐部"
#~ "里最多提升一两点质量。如此少见的拆分无法改变一场活动。只修正最离谱对阵的"
#~ "“客气”几乎毫无价值；收益要等到每一场对阵都被刻意平衡时才会出现，而这恰恰是"
#~ "社交场合中没人会做的事。"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:1034
#~ msgid ""
#~ "King of the court — winners move up a court and split, losers slide down, "
#~ "the bottom court rotates out — is the most interesting of the rating-free "
#~ "formats. It genuinely sorts: 57% quality in a typical club, six points "
#~ "over shuffling, and its constant mixing keeps the ladder honest where US-"
#~ "style starves it. But moving one court per round is simply too slow a "
#~ "matchmaker: day-to-day form reshuffles the courts faster than the ladder "
#~ "can sort them, and 72% of its games still start suboptimal. The court "
#~ "ladder is a rating system with one bit of memory — it rediscovers each "
#~ "player's level every night, from scratch."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "场地之王——胜者升一片场地并交换搭档，败者降场，最底层场地轮换下场——是不使用"
#~ "评分的模式中最有意思的一种。它确实能排序：在典型俱乐部中达到 57% 的质量，"
#~ "比随机洗牌高六个百分点，而其持续的搭档混合让阶梯保持真实，这一点上美式模式"
#~ "则相当欠缺。但每轮只移动一片场地，作为配对机制实在太慢：日常状态波动重排场"
#~ "地的速度快过阶梯排序的速度，仍有 72% 的比赛开局即为次优。场地阶梯是一个只"
#~ "有一位记忆的评分系统——它每晚都要从零开始重新发现每个人的水平。"

