#~ "club's life. I want to explore using score differentials to shorten them "
#~ "— potentially producing usable ratings within a round or two of an "
#~ "unrated player's first game. Currently the Round Robin tool already "
#~ "supports manually specified player rankings. The risk is that this is "
#~ "itself a form of oracle: reading more into a result than it actually says "
#~ "could tamper with convergence rather than speed it up."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "评分会持续精确 30–40 轮——即两到三场活动——虽然到第 5 轮配对质量就已优于基"
#~ "线，但真正冷启动的头十几轮仍是俱乐部生命中最艰难的阶段。我想探索利用比分差"
#~ "来缩短这一阶段——有可能在无评分球员打完一两场后就得出可用评分。目前循环赛工"
#~ "具已支持手动指定球员排名。风险在于这本身就是一种“先知”：从结果中读出超出其"
#~ "实际含义的信息，可能会干扰收敛而非加速收敛。"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:764
#~ msgid ""
#~ "Ratings pointing the wrong way: a strong player rated low, a weak player "
#~ "rated high. Strong players who take it easy on beginners can invert their "
#~ "own rating — unintentional sandbagging."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "评分方向错误：强的球员评分偏低，弱的球员评分偏高。对新手放水的强手可能会把"
#~ "自己的评分做反——无意中的“藏分”。"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:1184
#~ msgid ""
#~ "Scored rally by rally, true drubbings are rarer than the raw matchup "
#~ "numbers suggest — and matchmaking removes most of the ones that remain. "
#~ "In a typical club Competitive+ has blowouts down to 15% within a session "
#~ "and about 8% within two, settling at 7% against the Oracle's 4% floor. A "
#~ "varied club keeps a hard residue: Competitive+ bottoms out near 15% while "
#~ "the baseline sits at 33%, and even the Oracle blows out 7% — a ringer, a "
#~ "beginner and an off night make some drubbings unavoidable."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "若逐个回合计分，真正的一边倒比赛比原始对阵数字所显示的更少见——而配对又消除"
#~ "了其中的大部分。在典型俱乐部中，Competitive+ 在一次活动内把一边倒比赛降到 "
#~ "15%，两次活动内降到约 8%，最终稳定在 7%，而理论最优（Oracle）的下限是 4%。"
#~ "水平参差的俱乐部则留有难以消除的残余：Competitive+ 最低约 15%，而基准为 "
#~ "33%，即便是 Oracle 也有 7%——一名高手、一名新手加上一个状态不佳的夜晚，让部"
#~ "分一边倒比赛无法避免。"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:1186
#~ msgid ""
#~ "Since we can simulate the match quality effects of adding a player into "
#~ "an event, we can create an RSVP system that admits player based on their "
#~ "impact to the session, rather than the simple first-come-first-serve "
#~ "setups most events have."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "既然我们可以模拟某位球员加入活动后对对阵质量的影响，就可以建立一套报名系"
#~ "统，按球员对该场活动的影响来决定是否录取，而不是像大多数活动那样简单地先到"
#~ "先得。"

#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:786
#~ msgid ""
#~ "The baseline here is what open play actually deals: random courts that "
#~ "avoid repeating partners and opponents. (Measured against pure random, "
#~ "avoiding repeats changes match quality not at all — novelty buys variety "
#~ "and a slightly faster ladder, nothing else.) From a cold start, "
#~ "Competitive+ pulls away from it within the first handful of rounds — by "
#~ "round 5 its games are already measurably better, because every result "
#~ "moves a cold rating a long way. Even a club of all-unrated players gets "
#~ "value inside their first session, though in this club the early gain is "
#~ "match quality; the blowouts barely move in one session, because "
#~ "preventing a varied club's worst games takes ratings accurate enough to "
#~ "see them coming. With mature ratings the gap is decisive:"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "这里的基线就是开放打法实际的做法：随机分场，避免重复搭档和对手。（与纯随机"
#~ "相比，避免重复对对阵质量完全没有影响——新鲜感带来的是多样性和略快的排名收"
#~ "敛，别无其他。）从冷启动开始，Competitive+ 在最初几轮内就拉开差距——到第 5 "
#~ "轮其比赛质量已有可测量的提升，因为在评分尚“冷”时每个结果都会带来很大调整。"
#~ "即使是全员无评分的俱乐部，在第一场活动内就能获得价值，不过在这个俱乐部里早"
#~ "期收益体现在对阵质量上；一场活动内一边倒的比赛几乎没有减少，因为要防止差异"
#~ "大的俱乐部中最糟的比赛，需要足够准确的评分才能预见它们。评分成熟后，差距是"
#~ "决定性的："

